A||||24||87 Pegasus||What's It Like To Lose A Friend?||||9||
Z||000000||87 Pegasus||07-09-2001||01:34 AM||||I'm in the process of losing a friend.  She's not sick or anything...it's just...i think our friendship is growing apart, only I don't want it to.  I don't have many friends, and for me to lose one is losing alot.  I've been friends with her for 6 years, but alot has happened lately to discourage me.  I've been excluded from the family for things I normally wouldn't have, she said something to me that really hurt me, and I don't think she trusts me with her b.f.  I have NEVER given her the idea that I would EVER try to break her and her man up.  That is just something friends don't do.  But now what?  Has this happened to anyone?  Should I try to salvage this?  What do you do to feel better when your friend doesn't want to be your friend?<P>------------------<BR>Friends don't let friends drive Corvettes!!||||reg||9
Z||000001||DecadenceR||07-09-2001||01:38 AM||||I've had something similar happen to me with a few people. Sometimes it hurts more than others. but unfortunately, people do change. And when they change, you tend to grow apart. And as much as you'd like to stay and hold onto the friendship, sometimes you have to walk away to keep what little you do have. Sometimes it works out that you get close again later. But in the end, it's all for the best.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierobaby||07-09-2001||01:45 AM||||thats a though one...I've been in a similar situation... but it was me pushing the guy away...and I regret doing it... I love him dearly...but as it turns out I'm stupid and now miss him terribly... he got a bit jealous of my b/f and worried me...so I pushed him away...we still exchange a few words now and then...but its not the same<P>------------------<BR>1984 Sweet Candy Apple red Fiero sport coupe :-D<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Neal||07-09-2001||01:55 AM||||I dont really know the situation but ill say this,  Friends often need their space and as a friend your required to give it to them.  Dont think that she is giving up on the friendship just because she is pushing you away.<P>Give her the space she needs.  Instead of seeing her several times a week maybe talk on the phone 1or2 times a week, but DO NOT loose communication.  It is very important (especially with wemon) to let friends know you still care.  This way when she is ready to have a full time friend youll be back hardly missing anything.<P>Hope this helps, lemme know if the situation is different than i think.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87 Pegasus||07-09-2001||02:03 AM||||That's the thing...I don't talk to her now more than once a week, if that.  I have been giving her her space since April when she blew up on me.  I was hoping she would call me, but she's just been doing other things with other people instead of me.  It's like I'm not even there anymore.||||reg||13
Z||000005||Neal||07-09-2001||02:22 AM||||ye anow thats a tough call.  If it helps ill give you a personal example.<BR>Me and close friend of mine have been friends for about 15 years and we will go through phases somes times well meet for beers a couple times a week sometimes we may not even talk for a month or more.  But we will always be friends.<P>My worry is when she "blew up" on you it was over somthing very important to her and you didnt realize the significance untill it was to late.  I could suggest that you figure out an "im sorry" idea (if thats the case) that is relavent to the initial problem, that will hopefully tie up the problems.<P>Good friends are definitly hard to come by and are worth the effort, so fight for it without being pushy and nosey.  Possibly rely on your other friends, and try and hang out with an outside circle that you dont usually see and time should bring the two of you close again.||||reg||1
Z||000006||The Fieromaster||07-09-2001||02:26 AM||||To loose a friend....<BR>Well last year on the 24th of this month I lost a friend.. a guy who was actually more than a friend, closer than any brother... I wish that it was only that we stopped talkin.  But it was because he was killed!  It is the hardest thing that I have ever went through.  Even now typing this I am in tears remembering him and all those nights of Fiero cruisin we did... and Carlisle last year...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Id rather had gotten in a fight with him and not be talking to him now....<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">     <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||9
Z||000007||87 Pegasus||07-09-2001||02:28 AM||||When she blew up at me...i think it was because she was upset that I was hanging out with her man more than she was.  But I tried to explain to her....her man is just a friend first of all.  Second...I have no life.  I work and go home.  I talk to my bf and that's about it.  Her man had the same days off as I did, so instead of going home to sit in my room and avoid my mom's fiance, I would go and hang out with her man and his buddies because it also allowed me to meet new people.  I would also give her the space she and her man wanted.  I wasn't with him 24 hours a day.  When she blew up at me, five things came out at one time, but the first thing she said REALLY hurt me.  It was "I thought I didn't want you hanging out with my man unless I was around" that's harsh.  how am I supposed to take that?  That's why I'm not so quick to apologize.  She hurt me...bad.  I want her to realize that.||||reg||1
Z||000008||JohnnyK||07-09-2001||02:31 AM||||Losing a buddy? My best buddy drowned.. "Those acts of god really stick it in and break it off"||||reg||1
Z||000009||The Fieromaster||07-09-2001||02:35 AM||||JohnnyK...<P>Thats an understatement!!!  Sometimes I dont understand why god takes the best of em?  Why not the sicko rapist murderers first?<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">     <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000010||Neal||07-09-2001||02:43 AM||||I have a real good feeling that if/when she and her bf break up she will come running straight to you, but its pretty hard to wait for somthing like that.<P>Her not wanting you aroung her bf... sounds weird to me, maybe a jealousy issue?  she may not be as secure with him as she wants, and you may have been a threat (of stealing him?), which could be her grounds for what happened.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Galen||07-09-2001||04:03 AM||||Kinda wish I knew what it was like to have a friend. *cry* for the lonely G man has but a very few ..<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/redcreature.gif">   <BR><FONT SIZE="1">To whom it may concern, The preceeding message was the opinion of this person and not of this forum. If you do not like it. Oh well</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula88||07-09-2001||09:15 AM||||So far, it's hard.  I may be loosing the best friend I've ever had in my life right now.  She and I have been friends for years, and have (had) a connection unlike any I've ever experienced.  She could just instinctively know what I'm thinking.  I can't count how many times we both picked up the phone to call the other at the exact same time.  The trouble began after she got serious with her b/f.  He's way jealous of our friendship, and feels threatened by it.  He's either convinced she's cheating on him with me, or is just paranoid about it.  Problem is, as he's become a bigger part of her life, she's had less and less time for us.  That, of course, has made me react negatively as well.  I don't know where this will end for me.  Right now, we haven't spoken since she bailed out on me for my birthday (about 2.5 weeks ago).  We've exchanged a couple of emails, and she said she's still my best friend, but I'm hearing through the rumour mill that her boyfriend is telling people she's not talking to me anymore.  So at the moment, I'm at a loss as to what I can (or should) do.  And the prospect of losing her is a bleak future I don't want to envision.<P>That's not much help, I know, but you're not alone.  If that matters.||||reg||9
Z||000013||stimpy||07-09-2001||09:37 AM||||The way I look at it, hanging out with a friends significant other is just <B>begging</B> for trouble. It doesn't matter if that friend is being jealous or irrational, that is a recipe for misery for everyone.  Although your intentions may be pure, your friends boyfriend in some reptilian corner of his brain is thinking about some way of getting the chance to bag you without getting caught. There ain't no "just friends" with heterosexual males.  Some of us are more evolved then others, but deep down we're all dawgs. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Galen||07-09-2001||09:49 AM||||Stimpy, I thought you were a cat?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/redcreature.gif">   <BR><FONT SIZE="1">To whom it may concern, The preceeding message was the opinion of this person and not of this forum. If you do not like it. Oh well</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Formula88||07-09-2001||12:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>The way I look at it, hanging out with a friends significant other is just [b]begging</B> for trouble. [/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, if you were referring to my post, let me clarify.  I'm not hanging out with a friend's s.o.  My best friend has a significant other who is jealous of our friendship.  We were friends before she got involved with him.  ||||reg||1
Z||000016||JohnnyK||07-09-2001||02:19 PM||||Fieromaster: Let me give you my opinion on what has happened (to me at least).. "God" doesn't pick anyone.... ****  happens. But, in my own words, I have to suck it up.. ||||reg||1
